mode: "100644"
text: "# Pinterest SEO 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (search features + tools move).*\n\n## The POV: a visual search engine — keywords + relevance rank you, not followers\nPinterest is **\"Google with pictures\"** — a visual search engine (**631M MAU, Q1 2026**, **DA 94**, and pins\nalso rank in **Google image/web results**). **~97% of top searches are unbranded** (users search for what you\nsell without knowing who sells it). **Follower count barely matters; search optimization is everything.**\nPins have a **~4-month lifespan** (some 3–6 mo), so one optimized pin **compounds traffic for months** — ideal\nfor **evergreen** (recipes, decor, gift guides, tutorials).\n\n## Ranking factors\n**Domain quality + Pin quality + Pinner quality + relevance (keywords)** must align. **Engagement signals:\nsaves and long clicks (30+ sec on the destination) are the most important** (saves > clicks > views;\nscroll-past / hide / quick-bounce = negative). Pinterest reads **sequences of saves/clicks** to predict the\nuser's journey and serve related pins.\n\n## Keyword research (the foundation)\n- **Pinterest's own search-bar autocomplete** — type a seed; every suggestion is a real query. **Guided\n  Search bubbles** (the coloured pills under results — \"modern,\" \"budget,\" \"for beginners,\" \"2026\") =\n  long-tail modifiers, less competition. **Pinterest Trends (trends.pinterest.com) + Predicts** = seasonal\n  search volume + emerging trends.\n- **Long-tail (3+ words)** beats broad (\"easy dinner recipes for families\" > \"easy dinners\"). **Think like a\n  searcher**, not a marketer.\n\n## Where keywords go (keyword layering)\n- **Profile:** broad niche keywords in name + bio. **Boards:** keyword-rich **titles + descriptions**,\n  specific not cutesy (\"Minimalist Home Office Ideas,\" not \"Inspo Board\"). **Board semantic alignment matters\n  more in 2026** — a precise board (\"Keto Meal Prep for Beginners\") gives a pin far stronger ranking context\n  than a generic one (\"Healthy Food\"); save fresh pins to the relevant board first.\n- **Pin:** lead the **title** with the primary keyword — `[Primary Keyword] | [Secondary Benefit] | [Context]`\n  (≤100). A natural keyword-rich **description** (1–2 key phrases early, ~100–200 chars, **no stuffing**).\n  Plus **on-image/overlay text** (OCR-read), **alt text**, and a descriptive **image file name**.\n- **Alignment: Pin → Board → Page all reinforce the same keyword phrase** (clarity → ranking). **Rich Pins**\n  (pull live data from your site; require a **claimed site** + tag) boost trust/CTR.\n- **Hashtags are deprioritized** — keywords carry the ranking weight; at most 1–2 niche tags (or skip).\n\n## Fresh pins, clusters + cadence\n- **Fresh, keyword-optimized pins** (new images/URLs, **not repins/dupes**) — each is a **new chance to rank\n  for a new term.** 3–5/day is strong (top accounts 11–12); **volume without unique design/copy gets\n  suppressed** (quality scales with quantity or not at all).\n- **Publish related pins in clusters** so Pinterest connects the journey. **Seasonal: post 45–90 days ahead**\n  (users plan; time it with Trends). **Over-optimization is recognized + suppressed** — keep it natural.\n"
